1
00:00:02,384 --> 00:00:04,010
[footsteps running]

2
00:00:04,094 --> 00:00:06,430
[panting]

3
00:00:09,683 --> 00:00:11,435
[pleasant music playing]

4
00:00:14,104 --> 00:00:15,188
[cart wheels screeching]

5
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:24,197
[Taiki] <i>Every morning, there's one person...</i>

6
00:00:26,283 --> 00:00:28,201
<i>who I'm always dying to see.</i>

7
00:00:30,287 --> 00:00:32,289
[pants]

8
00:00:35,876 --> 00:00:36,960
<i>And that person is...</i>

9
00:00:38,336 --> 00:00:39,212
[gasps]

10
00:00:39,963 --> 00:00:40,964
[grunts]

11
00:00:44,718 --> 00:00:45,927
[Chinatsu] Are you okay?

12
00:00:47,137 --> 00:00:48,221
Yep, just fine.

13
00:00:48,305 --> 00:00:51,391
Sorry. I was practicing my elbow pass.

14
00:00:53,185 --> 00:00:54,352
Let me see.

15
00:00:56,188 --> 00:00:57,606
It's getting all red.

16
00:00:58,523 --> 00:01:00,609
- Probably hurt, huh?
- [gasps softly]

17
00:01:01,359 --> 00:01:03,403
[Taiki stutters] I'm fine, really!

18
00:01:03,487 --> 00:01:04,613
[Chinatsu] But...

19
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:06,615
Oh, I know.

20
00:01:07,866 --> 00:01:08,867
Take this.

21
00:01:12,245 --> 00:01:14,372
[Taiki] <i>She has a candy bar in her pocket.</i>

22
00:01:15,582 --> 00:01:17,167
[Chinatsu] And in return... [chuckles]

23
00:01:18,835 --> 00:01:19,878
forgive me.

24
00:01:19,961 --> 00:01:21,171
[exclaims]

25
00:01:22,214 --> 00:01:24,007
[Taiki] <i>Of course I forgive you!</i>

26
00:01:24,966 --> 00:01:26,551
EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

27
00:01:26,635 --> 00:01:30,013
[Taiki] <i>I go to Eimei, a private school
that's junior through senior high.</i>

28
00:01:30,096 --> 00:01:32,390
<i>It's got a powerhouse sports program.</i>

29
00:01:33,266 --> 00:01:35,602
<i>Since I graduated from junior high,</i>

30
00:01:36,102 --> 00:01:39,105
<i>I'm now practicing
with the high school badminton club.</i>

31
00:01:40,482 --> 00:01:43,652
<i>There's optional open practice
every morning,</i>

32
00:01:44,402 --> 00:01:47,155
<i>and I try to get there
earlier than anyone else.</i>

33
00:01:48,657 --> 00:01:50,450
<i>But she always beats me.</i>

34
00:01:51,034 --> 00:01:52,285
<i>Chinatsu Kano.</i>

35
00:01:54,704 --> 00:01:57,332
<i>Even before the gym
has warmed up for the day,</i>

36
00:01:57,415 --> 00:01:59,751
<i>she's there, shooting shot after shot.</i>

37
00:02:01,336 --> 00:02:03,421
<i>That's how Chinatsu is.</i>

38
00:02:04,172 --> 00:02:05,924
<i>That's why I like her.</i>

39
00:02:07,175 --> 00:02:09,010
[music fades]

40
00:02:12,097 --> 00:02:14,099
[opening theme song playing]

41
00:02:15,183 --> 00:02:18,436
BLUE BOX

42
00:03:34,596 --> 00:03:40,936
BLUE BOX

43
00:03:41,519 --> 00:03:45,565
EPISODE 1
CHINATSU SENPAI

44
00:03:45,649 --> 00:03:48,151
- [indistinct chatter]
- [whistle bowls]

45
00:03:48,235 --> 00:03:50,445
[chatter continues]

46
00:03:54,449 --> 00:03:55,575
[whistle bowls]

47
00:04:06,294 --> 00:04:07,420
[groans]

48
00:04:07,504 --> 00:04:09,297
I wanna marry her so bad.

49
00:04:09,381 --> 00:04:12,300
- [Kyo] Not gonna happen.
- [exclaims] Come on, bro!

50
00:04:12,384 --> 00:04:14,511
What, a wedding out of the blue?

51
00:04:14,594 --> 00:04:16,805
[Taiki] <i>Just think. I could see her face...</i>

52
00:04:16,888 --> 00:04:18,890
- Mornin'!
- [Taiki] <i>...first thing every morning.</i>

53
00:04:18,974 --> 00:04:21,268
<i>- It'd be awesome.</i>
- You want coffee?

54
00:04:21,351 --> 00:04:23,853
You couldn't even date her,
she's out of your league.

55
00:04:23,937 --> 00:04:24,771
[exclaims]

56
00:04:25,814 --> 00:04:28,858
[Kyo] <i>Not only is she
the basketball team's future MVP,</i>

57
00:04:29,693 --> 00:04:32,988
<i>she has talent, she's charismatic,
she's got the it factor.</i>

58
00:04:33,071 --> 00:04:34,197
TO THE HOOP WITH AGGRESSION!

59
00:04:34,281 --> 00:04:37,284
<i>And she's popular
inside and outside of school.</i>

60
00:04:37,367 --> 00:04:39,077
Then there's you, Taiki.

61
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:42,163
It may be that you're fine, at badminton,

62
00:04:42,247 --> 00:04:44,708
- but you aren't exactly popular.
- [exclaims]

63
00:04:44,791 --> 00:04:45,959
You're a bottom-rung player

64
00:04:46,042 --> 00:04:48,795
who's being allowed to practice
with the high schoolers.

65
00:04:48,878 --> 00:04:51,423
[groans]

66
00:04:51,506 --> 00:04:53,967
[Kyo] Like, if Chinatsu
was a ranked school,

67
00:04:54,050 --> 00:04:56,011
she'd be one of the top seeds.

68
00:04:56,094 --> 00:04:58,722
And your school
would lose in the first round.

69
00:04:58,805 --> 00:05:00,682
You're just on different levels.

70
00:05:01,641 --> 00:05:03,852
All you've got in common
is morning practice.

71
00:05:03,935 --> 00:05:07,605
We have other things in common!
You know, like my mom.

72
00:05:07,689 --> 00:05:10,108
She used to play basketball
for our school.

73
00:05:10,191 --> 00:05:12,944
A lot of legacy kids at private schools...

74
00:05:13,695 --> 00:05:16,364
[Taiki] I understand
where you're coming from, Kyo,

75
00:05:17,615 --> 00:05:20,952
but you also can't win unless you try!

76
00:05:21,745 --> 00:05:25,457
And you know what?
It's fun going up against the top schools.

77
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:29,961
Well, okay, then. See if you can
make it to the second round.

78
00:05:30,837 --> 00:05:32,630
You know, introduce yourself,

79
00:05:33,256 --> 00:05:34,799
or ask for her number.

80
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:36,718
All right.

81
00:05:36,801 --> 00:05:41,181
- What are you talking about?
- [grunts] What're you doing?

82
00:05:41,264 --> 00:05:43,475
I was just coming to say hi!

83
00:05:43,558 --> 00:05:45,435
[Taiki] What are you, a grade-schooler?

84
00:05:45,518 --> 00:05:49,481
I wish I was a kid, but as of spring,
I'll be in high school, same as you!

85
00:05:49,564 --> 00:05:51,191
I'll have you know,

86
00:05:51,274 --> 00:05:54,194
I've grown a whole seven centimeters
since we were in grade school.

87
00:05:54,277 --> 00:05:57,238
[Taiki] And yet you're still shorter
than the badminton net.

88
00:05:57,322 --> 00:05:58,364
Shut up!

89
00:05:58,448 --> 00:06:01,284
Oh, you're one to talk,
you're not that tall either!

90
00:06:01,367 --> 00:06:03,578
[grunting] I'm still growing! Okay?

91
00:06:03,661 --> 00:06:05,497
[Kyo] <i>Both of them are children.</i>

92
00:06:09,042 --> 00:06:11,002
[Hina] Anyway, something bothering you?

93
00:06:11,086 --> 00:06:13,254
Oh, no, don't worry about it.

94
00:06:15,757 --> 00:06:18,009
But, uh, just for the fun of it...

95
00:06:18,093 --> 00:06:19,511
What sort of things...

96
00:06:20,178 --> 00:06:22,764
can a guy do to attract a girl?

97
00:06:22,847 --> 00:06:25,517
Oh, is this a matter of love?

98
00:06:26,101 --> 00:06:29,020
I'm a one-stop-shop
for all that kinda stuff!

99
00:06:29,646 --> 00:06:31,773
For starters,
don't act like such a weenie.

100
00:06:31,856 --> 00:06:33,316
You need to show them

101
00:06:33,399 --> 00:06:35,777
that you're cool, calm,
collected, and reliable!

102
00:06:35,860 --> 00:06:39,030
And then, the most important of all is...

103
00:06:39,114 --> 00:06:40,198
{\an8}LIKE MARCE NGUYEN

104
00:06:40,281 --> 00:06:42,075
{\an8}...the body of a Greek god.

105
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:45,161
[exclaiming]

106
00:06:55,130 --> 00:06:57,298
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

107
00:06:57,382 --> 00:06:59,300
[creaking]

108
00:06:59,926 --> 00:07:02,262
[Taiki] <i>Asking for Hina's help
was a mistake.</i>

109
00:07:02,345 --> 00:07:04,514
<i>Her taste is too particular.</i>

110
00:07:05,765 --> 00:07:06,683
Huh?

111
00:07:10,019 --> 00:07:12,063
[serene music playing]

112
00:07:12,814 --> 00:07:15,442
<i>I guess they haven't unlocked
the gym doors yet.</i>

113
00:07:24,784 --> 00:07:27,203
<i>Okay. Now's my chance.</i>

114
00:07:27,871 --> 00:07:29,372
<i>I gotta talk to her!</i>

115
00:07:30,290 --> 00:07:32,417
[heart beating]

116
00:07:34,294 --> 00:07:37,589
<i>I'll introduce myself.
Er, that might be weird, out of nowhere.</i>

117
00:07:37,672 --> 00:07:39,174
THIS AIN'T NO JOB INTERVIEW

118
00:07:39,257 --> 00:07:41,301
<i>Maybe thank her for the candy bar?</i>

119
00:07:41,384 --> 00:07:43,219
<i>Then again, I haven't eaten it yet.</i>

120
00:07:43,303 --> 00:07:44,220
I OFFER MY THANKS

121
00:07:44,304 --> 00:07:45,805
<i>Oh, I got it!</i>

122
00:07:45,889 --> 00:07:47,682
<i>I'll ask her what she's reading.</i>

123
00:07:48,558 --> 00:07:50,351
RUNNING A STACK PLAY

124
00:07:50,977 --> 00:07:52,020
[exclaims softly]

125
00:07:57,233 --> 00:07:59,319
<i>I'll just keep quiet I guess.</i>

126
00:08:00,195 --> 00:08:02,113
- [Chinatsu sneezes]
- [gasps]

127
00:08:02,697 --> 00:08:06,534
Uh, um... If you'd like,
you can wear my scarf!

128
00:08:06,618 --> 00:08:08,495
It's fresh from the laundry!

129
00:08:10,288 --> 00:08:13,166
And then... I have hot tea.

130
00:08:13,666 --> 00:08:16,252
This thermos is really good
at keeping things warm!

131
00:08:16,336 --> 00:08:19,130
And also, I have gloves and a hand warmer!

132
00:08:19,714 --> 00:08:21,466
It heats when you shake it!

133
00:08:26,012 --> 00:08:27,805
<i>I've done it now.</i>

134
00:08:27,889 --> 00:08:29,724
<i>I word vomited!</i>

135
00:08:31,434 --> 00:08:33,394
- [chuckles softly]
- [Taiki exclaims]

136
00:08:34,229 --> 00:08:36,147
Wha... what is it?

137
00:08:36,231 --> 00:08:39,484
Nothing, I'm just wondering what
you're going to offer me next, that's all.

138
00:08:39,567 --> 00:08:41,444
[grunts nervously]

139
00:08:41,528 --> 00:08:42,654
[amusing music playing]

140
00:08:43,738 --> 00:08:46,366
[giggles] I was just kidding.

141
00:08:48,243 --> 00:08:49,869
Thanks for watching out for me.

142
00:08:50,453 --> 00:08:51,663
Uh... Sure!

143
00:08:51,746 --> 00:08:54,165
<i>She laughed!</i> [sneezes]

144
00:08:58,545 --> 00:09:01,965
You don't have to worry about me.
You keep yourself warm.

145
00:09:06,844 --> 00:09:08,179
[Taiki] <i>This feels like...</i>

146
00:09:09,264 --> 00:09:13,184
<i>when a wife...
ties her newlywed husband's tie.</i>

147
00:09:14,811 --> 00:09:16,354
- Sorry.
- It's fine.

148
00:09:18,314 --> 00:09:19,983
<i>I've always thought...</i>

149
00:09:20,608 --> 00:09:23,570
<i>Chinatsu would have
a low body temperature.</i>

150
00:09:25,029 --> 00:09:26,072
All done.

151
00:09:26,823 --> 00:09:29,701
- Sorry, I'm running behind this morning!
- [Chinatsu] No worries.

152
00:09:30,326 --> 00:09:31,661
Don't catch a cold, okay?

153
00:09:32,287 --> 00:09:33,830
Taiki Inomata.

154
00:09:33,913 --> 00:09:36,040
[gasps] How do you know my name?

155
00:09:36,708 --> 00:09:38,710
Well, how do you think?

156
00:09:39,294 --> 00:09:40,420
[gasps]

157
00:09:41,004 --> 00:09:43,590
[Taiki] <i>Hang on.
Has she always known my name?</i>

158
00:09:43,673 --> 00:09:44,716
You have a good mom.

159
00:09:46,134 --> 00:09:47,969
[Taiki] <i>Good mom?</i> [exclaims]

160
00:09:48,052 --> 00:09:48,970
TAIKI INOMATA

161
00:09:49,053 --> 00:09:51,848
<i>So embarrassing!
Well, at least she said my name.</i>

162
00:09:51,931 --> 00:09:53,266
[whimpers]

163
00:09:54,851 --> 00:09:58,896
<i>Nope, it's still embarrassing!</i>

164
00:10:04,569 --> 00:10:06,487
[players grunting]

165
00:10:10,366 --> 00:10:11,492
[grunts]

166
00:10:11,576 --> 00:10:13,286
- Good effort dude!
- Nice serve!

167
00:10:13,369 --> 00:10:14,454
Take a break!

168
00:10:14,537 --> 00:10:17,915
[boy] Phew! Taiki.
Could you go wet the rags?

169
00:10:17,999 --> 00:10:18,916
[Taiki] Yes!

170
00:10:19,542 --> 00:10:21,461
[water running]

171
00:10:22,295 --> 00:10:25,465
[Taiki] <i>The good thing is
she knows my name now.</i>

172
00:10:26,090 --> 00:10:27,467
[Chinatsu] <i>Taiki Inomata.</i>

173
00:10:29,469 --> 00:10:33,473
[Taiki] <i>Hearing her say it hit me
a lot harder than I expected it to.</i>

174
00:10:33,556 --> 00:10:35,266
[laughs]

175
00:10:36,059 --> 00:10:36,976
[clears throat]

176
00:10:38,186 --> 00:10:41,105
<i>Anyway, I've made it
past the second round.</i>

177
00:10:41,814 --> 00:10:44,275
<i>Now it's time for round number three.</i>

178
00:10:44,776 --> 00:10:47,236
<i>I'm going to ask for her number!</i>

179
00:10:54,619 --> 00:10:57,997
[Taiki] <i>The coach of the girls'
basketball team and Chinatsu?</i>

180
00:10:59,248 --> 00:11:01,918
- Whatcha looking at?
- [yelps] Hina!

181
00:11:02,001 --> 00:11:04,796
- I wasn't looking at anything.
- [Hina gasps]

182
00:11:04,879 --> 00:11:06,506
- Hm.
- [Taiki grunts nervously]

183
00:11:07,590 --> 00:11:09,634
Don't shoot too high, Taiki.

184
00:11:10,176 --> 00:11:11,761
[Taiki] <i>Like you're the expert.</i>

185
00:11:12,595 --> 00:11:15,932
It's not that.
She just looked really serious.

186
00:11:16,015 --> 00:11:17,266
That's all.

187
00:11:17,350 --> 00:11:18,518
[Hina sighs]

188
00:11:19,727 --> 00:11:23,606
You know the other day, I saw her walking
with another guy, just the two of them.

189
00:11:23,689 --> 00:11:24,774
[gasps]

190
00:11:24,857 --> 00:11:26,109
[giggles]

191
00:11:27,568 --> 00:11:28,945
JK!

192
00:11:29,487 --> 00:11:31,197
[humming]

193
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:33,408
[Taiki] <i>What a jerk!</i>

194
00:11:33,491 --> 00:11:35,576
[footsteps approaching]

195
00:11:35,660 --> 00:11:36,577
[Taiki] Mm.

196
00:11:38,496 --> 00:11:40,039
[inaudible]

197
00:11:45,753 --> 00:11:47,964
- [boy 1] Ah, I'm tired.
- [boy 2] Nice hustle!

198
00:11:48,047 --> 00:11:49,549
- See you tomorrow.
- Yeah, see ya!

199
00:11:49,632 --> 00:11:50,591
I'm heading out!

200
00:11:50,675 --> 00:11:52,260
Have a good night, y'all!

201
00:11:52,343 --> 00:11:53,594
[all] Have a good night!

202
00:11:55,096 --> 00:11:56,097
Oh.

203
00:11:56,722 --> 00:11:58,850
[Taiki] <i>I forgot my towel in the gym.</i>

204
00:11:59,767 --> 00:12:01,436
What, did you forget something?

205
00:12:01,519 --> 00:12:03,521
- Yeah, go on--
- I'll head out.

206
00:12:03,604 --> 00:12:04,605
[Taiki sighs]

207
00:12:07,859 --> 00:12:10,111
[Taiki] <i>Oh, good. It's still open.</i>

208
00:12:12,697 --> 00:12:14,615
- [ball dribbling]
- [gasps softly]

209
00:12:14,699 --> 00:12:15,950
[uplifting music playing]

210
00:12:19,537 --> 00:12:22,623
[Taiki] <i>I can't believe it.
She's... still at it.</i>

211
00:12:24,125 --> 00:12:25,376
[Chinatsu] Taiki Inomata.

212
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:27,962
[Taiki exclaims] <i>She remembered my name!</i>

213
00:12:29,255 --> 00:12:30,882
You're still here practicing?

214
00:12:31,799 --> 00:12:35,052
[Chinatsu] I wasn't happy
with how I played during practice today.

215
00:12:35,136 --> 00:12:37,388
[Taiki] There is such a thing
as overdoing it.

216
00:12:37,472 --> 00:12:39,682
That may be true but...

217
00:12:39,765 --> 00:12:43,144
right now, I wanna get
as much time on the court as I can.

218
00:12:44,979 --> 00:12:47,064
[Taiki] <i>She really does love basketball.</i>

219
00:12:49,734 --> 00:12:51,402
[exclaims] <i>She caught me staring.</i>

220
00:12:53,529 --> 00:12:54,906
Let's play one-on-one!

221
00:12:55,531 --> 00:12:56,657
Okay?

222
00:12:57,992 --> 00:12:59,243
[Taiki grunting]

223
00:13:04,373 --> 00:13:05,541
[Taiki grunts]

224
00:13:05,625 --> 00:13:07,335
[breathing heavily]

225
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:11,088
Why don't we take a little break.

226
00:13:11,172 --> 00:13:13,299
I'm so... [coughs] sorry.

227
00:13:14,258 --> 00:13:15,801
<i>I'm pathetic.</i>

228
00:13:16,427 --> 00:13:18,554
[Chinatsu] No denying
you're a badminton player.

229
00:13:18,638 --> 00:13:19,805
You move well on the court.

230
00:13:20,515 --> 00:13:22,808
My mom used to be on the basketball team,

231
00:13:22,892 --> 00:13:25,394
so I would play with her
when I was growing up.

232
00:13:25,478 --> 00:13:26,812
Wow, same!

233
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:29,815
My mom was on the basketball team.

234
00:13:29,899 --> 00:13:33,819
Before I joined the youth team,
the two of us would play together.

235
00:13:33,903 --> 00:13:36,822
[Taiki] <i>We have something in common.
It's fate!</i>

236
00:13:37,532 --> 00:13:40,326
Did you ever think
about playing basketball?

237
00:13:40,409 --> 00:13:41,786
[yelling]

238
00:13:41,869 --> 00:13:42,745
Pass it!

239
00:13:43,496 --> 00:13:46,999
I think that team sports
are maybe not my thing.

240
00:13:47,083 --> 00:13:48,000
Gotcha.

241
00:13:48,834 --> 00:13:51,254
Besides, I like badminton.

242
00:13:52,255 --> 00:13:55,299
<i>How it's just me out on the court,</i>

243
00:13:55,383 --> 00:13:57,927
<i>and I'm in control of the match's outcome.</i>

244
00:14:00,054 --> 00:14:04,183
Whether I win or lose,
I can only thank or blame myself.

245
00:14:04,267 --> 00:14:06,185
I enjoy that kind of pressure.

246
00:14:06,852 --> 00:14:09,230
- You're a masochist.
- [exclaims]

247
00:14:09,855 --> 00:14:11,023
[chuckles softly]

248
00:14:11,732 --> 00:14:13,192
But I get it now.

249
00:14:13,818 --> 00:14:16,112
That's why you're always
practicing so hard.

250
00:14:16,195 --> 00:14:17,989
[ball dribbling]

251
00:14:18,614 --> 00:14:20,533
Well, coming from you...

252
00:14:21,033 --> 00:14:22,785
I meant it as a compliment.

253
00:14:22,869 --> 00:14:24,287
Well, I mean...

254
00:14:25,246 --> 00:14:26,914
you were here practicing

255
00:14:26,998 --> 00:14:29,917
the day after you graduated
from your junior high club.

256
00:14:31,085 --> 00:14:32,295
[Chinatsu exclaims]

257
00:14:32,378 --> 00:14:34,547
Must've been a year and a half ago.

258
00:14:36,132 --> 00:14:38,050
{\an8}<i>I didn't have practice that day...</i>

259
00:14:39,010 --> 00:14:41,554
<i>but I had some equipment
I needed to return...</i>

260
00:14:41,637 --> 00:14:43,055
<i>and I live close by...</i>

261
00:14:43,139 --> 00:14:45,600
<i>- so I came anyway.</i>
- [ball dribbling]

262
00:14:45,683 --> 00:14:47,059
<i>When I got there...</i>

263
00:14:47,894 --> 00:14:49,687
[mellow music playing]

264
00:15:00,072 --> 00:15:04,243
<i>I heard later that your team
had narrowly missed the cut for nationals.</i>

265
00:15:05,828 --> 00:15:07,830
That must've been frustrating for you.

266
00:15:08,497 --> 00:15:13,085
Seeing that you worked so hard,
and only to end up disappointed.

267
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:16,380
It made me want to work that hard, too.

268
00:15:18,925 --> 00:15:20,760
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

269
00:15:20,843 --> 00:15:24,430
<i>that was probably what made me
like her in the first place.</i>

270
00:15:30,686 --> 00:15:31,812
[gasps]

271
00:15:34,857 --> 00:15:36,233
I'd forgotten that.

272
00:15:39,862 --> 00:15:43,366
Okay! The two of you
should be heading home now!

273
00:15:43,449 --> 00:15:44,659
Okay!

274
00:15:45,159 --> 00:15:46,452
Let's clean up first.

275
00:15:47,203 --> 00:15:48,412
[Taiki] <i>That's weird.</i>

276
00:15:48,913 --> 00:15:51,123
<i>For a second, I thought she was crying.</i>

277
00:16:05,805 --> 00:16:06,889
Thanks for your help.

278
00:16:07,473 --> 00:16:08,599
[gasps softly]

279
00:16:09,642 --> 00:16:10,893
Oh, sure.

280
00:16:16,857 --> 00:16:19,110
<i>Maybe it's 'cause we were just playing...</i>

281
00:16:21,445 --> 00:16:22,655
<i>but her hand...</i>

282
00:16:23,322 --> 00:16:25,408
<i>felt warmer than last time.</i>

283
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,710
[birds chirping]

284
00:16:39,005 --> 00:16:41,924
<i>It'll mostly be sunny
throughout the country today.</i>

285
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,760
- Mornin'.
- Good morning.

286
00:16:44,844 --> 00:16:47,430
- Lunch is on the table.
- Yeah, thanks, Mom.

287
00:16:48,389 --> 00:16:50,433
You're not wearing your sweatshirt?

288
00:16:50,516 --> 00:16:52,184
Nah, it's warm today.

289
00:16:52,727 --> 00:16:54,770
But I went out of my way to wash it.

290
00:16:54,854 --> 00:16:56,480
Sorry, sorry. [exclaims]

291
00:16:57,273 --> 00:16:59,442
GOING STRAIGHT FOR THE NET!
CHINATSU KANO

292
00:17:00,067 --> 00:17:01,277
{\an8}Chinatsu!

293
00:17:01,944 --> 00:17:03,320
{\an8}Oh, you know her?

294
00:17:03,404 --> 00:17:04,947
What? Uh, no, I don't.

295
00:17:05,948 --> 00:17:09,577
Actually, Chinatsu's mom and I
were on the same team,

296
00:17:09,660 --> 00:17:11,871
<i>and played basketball together
back in the day.</i>

297
00:17:11,954 --> 00:17:15,166
- What?!
- Why the yelling all of a sudden?

298
00:17:15,833 --> 00:17:16,959
No reason.

299
00:17:17,710 --> 00:17:19,920
{\an8}<i>We have so much in common!</i>

300
00:17:21,088 --> 00:17:23,466
[Taiki's mom] We've been in touch
on and off over the years,

301
00:17:24,175 --> 00:17:28,471
but I wouldn't have expected Chinatsu
to become such an impressive young person!

302
00:17:29,096 --> 00:17:32,975
It's too bad, though.
I heard they're moving overseas for work.

303
00:17:39,565 --> 00:17:42,651
Word on the street is
they're going to move in mid-March.

304
00:17:42,735 --> 00:17:44,487
It's such a bummer.

305
00:17:44,570 --> 00:17:46,489
[emotional music playing]

306
00:17:47,531 --> 00:17:49,533
[Taiki] <i>Now that she mentions it...</i>

307
00:17:50,117 --> 00:17:51,118
[grunts]

308
00:17:52,620 --> 00:17:53,537
Taiki?

309
00:17:55,498 --> 00:17:57,875
[Taiki] <i>Moving? Overseas?</i>

310
00:17:57,958 --> 00:18:00,669
<i>What? This can't be happening.</i>

311
00:18:00,753 --> 00:18:02,505
[panting]

312
00:18:04,173 --> 00:18:06,008
[grunts]

313
00:18:06,092 --> 00:18:08,469
<i>She can't possibly be okay with that!</i>

314
00:18:09,970 --> 00:18:12,098
<i>She's the first one there every day.</i>

315
00:18:13,182 --> 00:18:14,850
<i>She practices more than anyone.</i>

316
00:18:16,227 --> 00:18:19,522
<i>Even when... she was at her lowest!</i>

317
00:18:21,107 --> 00:18:24,401
<i>All her passion...
the effort that she's put in...</i>

318
00:18:24,485 --> 00:18:27,363
<i>her goals, her dreams, everything!</i>

319
00:18:27,988 --> 00:18:30,116
<i>Can she really leave all that behind?</i>

320
00:18:38,124 --> 00:18:39,750
[door opens]

321
00:18:39,834 --> 00:18:41,418
[Taiki panting]

322
00:18:46,799 --> 00:18:47,633
Taiki.

323
00:18:48,926 --> 00:18:50,427
Are you okay?

324
00:18:50,928 --> 00:18:54,640
Please, Chinatsu,
you have to go to nationals.

325
00:18:57,017 --> 00:19:00,146
You... you're the one who taught me that...

326
00:19:00,896 --> 00:19:03,899
you need to work toward
your goal every day.

327
00:19:03,983 --> 00:19:07,778
And that even if you lose,
you keep moving forward.

328
00:19:08,737 --> 00:19:11,657
- So... please don't give up.
- [music intensifies]

329
00:19:12,783 --> 00:19:14,451
It's not your fault

330
00:19:14,535 --> 00:19:17,663
that your parents are
getting transferred overseas for work.

331
00:19:17,746 --> 00:19:19,665
- That is just--
- Sorry.

332
00:19:19,748 --> 00:19:22,042
I'm not going overseas.

333
00:19:22,126 --> 00:19:23,210
[music stops]

334
00:19:23,752 --> 00:19:24,920
Huh?

335
00:19:26,255 --> 00:19:28,048
Um... Uh... Wait...

336
00:19:29,049 --> 00:19:32,094
To be specific,
my family is going overseas,

337
00:19:32,178 --> 00:19:33,554
but I'm going to stay here.

338
00:19:33,637 --> 00:19:35,890
A family friend
is letting me live with them.

339
00:19:36,390 --> 00:19:38,475
[Taiki] <i>Which means... I...</i>

340
00:19:39,268 --> 00:19:42,062
<i>word vomited again!</i>

341
00:19:42,771 --> 00:19:44,481
Oh, then that's cool!

342
00:19:44,565 --> 00:19:46,567
- [Chinatsu] I was pretty conflicted.
- [exclaims]

343
00:19:48,319 --> 00:19:50,946
I know it'll be sad
being away from my family.

344
00:19:52,156 --> 00:19:53,449
But...

345
00:19:53,532 --> 00:19:55,034
I was reminded...

346
00:19:55,743 --> 00:19:58,954
of the time when I graduated
from my junior high team.

347
00:20:00,039 --> 00:20:02,958
I still want to go to nationals.

348
00:20:04,668 --> 00:20:06,837
I don't want to give up on that dream.

349
00:20:12,301 --> 00:20:13,969
And it's all because of you.

350
00:20:14,803 --> 00:20:17,765
Thank you, Taiki Inomata!

351
00:20:23,187 --> 00:20:25,731
I didn't... do anything.

352
00:20:28,484 --> 00:20:30,152
You up for more one-on-one?

353
00:20:30,819 --> 00:20:32,821
[pleasant guitar music playing]

354
00:20:34,949 --> 00:20:37,201
[Taiki] Why don't we
play badminton this time?

355
00:20:37,284 --> 00:20:38,452
[Chinatsu] Sure thing!

356
00:20:46,335 --> 00:20:48,254
[birds chirping]

357
00:20:51,090 --> 00:20:53,008
SUNDAY

358
00:20:53,926 --> 00:20:55,052
[Taiki] <i>Wait.</i>

359
00:20:55,135 --> 00:20:57,888
<i>I embarrassed myself
the other day, didn't I?</i>

360
00:20:58,597 --> 00:21:00,766
[grunts in frustration]

361
00:21:08,232 --> 00:21:10,526
<i>I'm so glad that today is Sunday.</i>

362
00:21:16,156 --> 00:21:19,034
<i>This may actually be the first time...</i>

363
00:21:21,078 --> 00:21:23,122
<i>that I don't wanna see...</i>

364
00:21:23,622 --> 00:21:25,249
[birds chirping]

365
00:21:27,042 --> 00:21:28,294
Morning.

366
00:21:28,377 --> 00:21:30,796
[gasps]

367
00:21:31,547 --> 00:21:35,050
[Taiki] <i>Why... why is Chinatsu in my house?</i>

368
00:21:36,135 --> 00:21:37,136
[gasps]

369
00:21:37,219 --> 00:21:39,555
Good morning, Taiki. I see you're up.

370
00:21:39,638 --> 00:21:40,764
Ah!

371
00:21:40,848 --> 00:21:42,558
I mentioned her before.

372
00:21:43,183 --> 00:21:45,561
This is Chinatsu Kano.

373
00:21:46,687 --> 00:21:49,315
Starting in the spring,
she'll be living with us.

374
00:21:49,857 --> 00:21:52,818
Thank you for letting Chinatsu
stay with you. It means a lot.

375
00:21:52,901 --> 00:21:55,070
- Yes, thank you.
- Once teammates, always teammates!

376
00:21:55,154 --> 00:21:56,155
[gasps]

377
00:21:56,238 --> 00:21:58,574
[Taiki's and Chinatsu's moms]
We are Eimei!

378
00:21:59,658 --> 00:22:03,746
[Taiki] <i>Is this for real?!</i>

379
00:22:05,456 --> 00:22:07,458
[closing theme song playing]
